//! rlibc-x: A minimal, Rust-based libc implementation for Linux x86_64
//!
//! This crate provides the minimal runtime support needed to build
//! standalone Rust binaries that don't depend on glibc or any external libc.
//!
//! ## Features
//!
//! - Direct syscalls for Linux x86_64
//! - Program entry point (_start)
//! - Basic memory allocation via brk()
//! - Process termination (exit)
//!
//! ## Usage
//!
//! In your `#![no_std]` `#![no_main]` binary, add rlibc-x as a dependency.
